Let Stop take back a message waiting for its session's sandbox to start.

A message for a session whose sandbox is still starting waits in its POST
(_await_settled_managed_launch) and goes to the agent once the sandbox is
up. Upstream's web UI kept a Claude Code session's first message in the
browser for that whole start, so Stop could still take it back; on a phone,
closing the app during the start lost the message. The web UI now posts it
straight away (web-patches/0029-first-message-while-starting.patch), so the
server has to be the one that takes it back: Stop (an interrupt) during the
start sets an event each waiting message watches, and the message answers
409 "Stopped before the sandbox started" instead of being sent. A message
sent after Stop waits as usual.

The waiting POST already outlives its client: Starlette doesn't cancel a
handler that isn't reading the request when the client disconnects. The test
covers that too, on the Starlette the server image resolves.
Base: omnigent v0.18.0 (a8676d23e88d), after 0019-mcp-servers.patch.
